      "id": "mJ4QzWn7RZmcf23I",
      "productId": "openmrs",
      "question": "When a user saves the fulfiller status and comment of a lab order in the patient chart, what code runs from the frontend request down to the database write? List the frontend function that sends the request, the server-side REST handler, the core service implementation, and the data-access method.",
      "generation": "g-b59a21",
      "kind": "partial",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Saving the fulfiller status/comment from the lab results form goes **frontend form → REST sub-resource → core service → DAO → Hibernate**.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**1. Frontend function that sends the request**\n- The submit handler is `saveLabResults` in the exported lab results workspace; for a new save it calls `updateOrderResult` [1], and for an edit / resumed attempt it calls `completeOrderWithSavedResults` [2].\n- The status and comment come from `resultsStatusPayload` (`fulfillerStatus: 'COMPLETED'`, `fulfillerComment: 'Test Results Entered'`) [3].\n- Both paths end in `updateOrderFulfillerDetails`, which POSTs the payload to `${restBaseUrl}/order/${orderUuid}/fulfillerdetails/` [4]. Note this is a **second** request: `updateOrderResult` first POSTs the encounter observation/order payload [5] and only then calls the fulfiller-details call.",
          "citations": [
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4,
            5
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2. Server-side REST handler**\n- The route is registered by the `@SubResource` on `FulfillerDetailsResource2_3` (path `fulfillerdetails`, parent `OrderResource2_2`) [6].\n- The handler is the resource's `save(FulfillerDetails2_3)` method [7], which maps the JSON body onto the `FulfillerDetails2_3` delegate (`fulfillerStatus`, `fulfillerComment`, `accessionNumber`) [8] and calls the service.",
          "citations": [
            6,
            7,
            8
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**3. Core service implementation**\n- `OrderServiceImpl.updateOrderFulfillerStatus(Order, FulfillerStatus, String, String)` [9]: it sets the fulfiller status / comment / accession number on the `Order` (only for non-null arguments), then calls `saveOrderInternal` [10]. The 2-arg overload just delegates with a null accession number [11].",
          "citations": [
            9,
            10,
            11
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**4. Data-access method**\n- `saveOrderInternal` ends with `dao.saveOrder(order)` [12], declared on `OrderDAO` api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/db/OrderDAO.java and implemented by `HibernateOrderDAO.saveOrder`, which is the actual write: `HibernateUtil.saveOrUpdate(sessionFactory.getCurrentSession(), order)` api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/db/hibernate/HibernateOrderDAO.java.",
          "citations": [
            12
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "```mermaid\n---\ntitle: Lab order fulfiller status save path\n---\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Form as saveLabResults (workspace)\n  participant Res as lab-results.resource.ts\n  participant REST as FulfillerDetailsResource2_3\n  participant Svc as OrderServiceImpl\n  participant DAO as HibernateOrderDAO\n  participant DB as Database\n  Form->>Res: updateOrderResult / completeOrderWithSavedResults\n  Res->>REST: POST /order/{uuid}/fulfillerdetails\n  REST->>Svc: updateOrderFulfillerStatus\n  Svc->>Svc: saveOrderInternal\n  Svc->>DAO: saveOrder\n  DAO->>DB: saveOrUpdate\n```",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "One caveat: the exact HTTP controller class that publishes the sub-resource route lives in the webservices.rest module's framework (the `@SubResource` annotation is the registration point here); I only saw test classes named `FulfillerDetailsController2_3Test`, not a hand-written controller for this route.",
          "citations": []
        }
      ],
